ion?\" So first two rounds: each of which had 6 matches. So two rounds, each 6 matches. So that's 12 matches. Then the last round: 4 matches total. He wins half, so 2 matches. So total 12 + 2 = 14. So answer is \\boxed{14}.\n\nTherefore, the number of matches won is 14 presented in boxed notation.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{14}\n</think>\n\nBrendan winning all matches in the first two rounds means that he won 6 matches in each of those rounds, totaling $6 + 6 = 12$ matches. Then, he wins half of the 4 matches in the last round, so he won $2 = 4 / 2$. Adding these, the total matches won throughout the competition is $12 + 2 = 14$. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55843, 702, 10636, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 323, 14816, 9071