otal slices**: Adding both contributions:\n   $$\n   30 \\text{ slices} + 15 \\text{ slices} = 45 \\text{ slices}\n   $$\n\nThus, the total number of watermelon slices in the picnic is $\\boxed{45}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Danny brings 3 watermelons to his family picnic. He cuts each watermelon into 10 slices. His sister brings 1 watermelon to the family picnic, and she cuts the watermelon into 15 slices. How many watermelon slices are there in total at the picnic?", "answer": "From Danny, there are 3 * 10 = <<3*10=30>>30 watermelon slices\nFrom his sister, there are 1 * 15 = <<1*15=15>>15 watermelon slices\nThere are a total of 30 + 15 = <<30+15=45>>45 watermelon slices\n#### 45", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Danny brings 3 watermelons to his family picnic. He cuts each watermelon into 10 slices. His sister brings 1 watermelon to the family picnic, and she cuts the watermelon into 15 slices. How many watermelon slices are there in total at the picnic?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["45"], "solution": "45"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 32599, 12434, 220, 18, 3015, 27127, 2382, 311, 806, 2997, 54462, 13, 1260, 15104, 1817, 3015, 71118, 1119, 220, 16, 15, 34254, 13, 5301, 12923, 12434, 220, 16, 3015, 71118, 311, 279, 2997, 54462, 11, 323, 1340], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 32599, 7117, 220, 18, 3015, 27127, 2382, 11, 1290, 30, 8886, 315, 1846, 3015, 27127, 2382, 572, 3931, 1119, 220, 16, 15, 34254, 13, 2055, 11, 1156, 11, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 34254, 32599, 594, 3015, 27127, 2382, 16792, 13, 1260, 702, 220, 18, 3015, 27127, 2382, 13, 8886, 374, 220, 16, 15]}
