2026-10-30 05:46:17 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 9, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: The New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize its squares. But they don't have enough squares to use all the streetlights bought. Knowing that there are 15 squares in New York and that each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council, how many unused streetlights will remain?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: The New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize its squares. But they don't have enough squares to use all the streetlights bought. Knowing that there are 15 squares in New York and that each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council, how many unused streetlights will remain?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The problem says the New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize their squares. But they can't use all of them because there are only 15 squares. Each park needs 12 new streetlights, and we need to find how many unused streetlights remain.\n\nFirst, I need to figure out how many streetlights will be used to cover the squares. There are 15 squares. Each square needs 12 streetlights. Wait, does each square need exactly 12 streetlights? The problem says \"each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council\", so there are 15 squares in New York. So, if there are 15 squares, and each square needs 12 streetlights, then total streetlights needed would be 15 times 12. Let me check that.\n\n15 squares * 12 new streetlights each park = 180 streetlights. But they bought 200 streetlights. So if they only need 180, how many are left unused? That would be 200 - 180 = 20. So the answer is \\boxed{20}?\n\nWait, let me verify again. If there are 15 squares, and each square needs 12 streetlight, then total needed is 15*12 = 180. The council has 200, so 200 - 180 = 20 left. Yes, so the answer is \\boxed{20} in the box. I think that's right. Let me just double-check the multiplication.\n\n15 squares times 12 streetlights per square equals 180. 180 is definitely less than 200. Therefore, 200 minus 180 is 20, so the unused are 20 streetlights. So the answer is \\boxed{20}. Since the problem says to put the final answer in \\boxed{} and the problem is about streetlights, maybe in the box as \\boxed{20} with the \\boxed{} brackets. So the answer is \\boxed{20}.\n</think>\n\nThe problem states that there are 15 squares in New York and each has 12 new streetlights. Total streetlights needed for the squares: $15 \\times 12 = 180$. Since the council bought 200 streetlights, the unused are $200 - 180 = \\boxed{20}$. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{20}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "The New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize its squares. But they don't have enough squares to use all the streetlights bought. Knowing that there are 15 squares in New York and that each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council, how many unused streetlights will remain?", "answer": "So the total number of streetlights that will be used is 15 squares * 12 streetlights/square = <<15*12=180>>180 streetlights\nThere will be 200 streetlights - 180 streetlights = <<200-180=20>>20 streetlights unused.\n#### 20", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: The New York City Council bought 200 streetlights to modernize its squares. But they don't have enough squares to use all the streetlights bought. Knowing that there are 15 squares in New York and that each park will have 12 new streetlights bought by the city council, how many unused streetlights will remain?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["20"], "solution": "20"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 576, 1532, 4261, 4311, 9074, 10788, 220, 17, 15, 15, 8592, 13826, 311, 6481, 551, 1181, 31340, 13, 1988, 807, 1513, 944, 614, 3322, 31340, 311, 990, 678, 279, 8592, 13826, 10788, 13, 57633, 429, 1052, 525], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 279, 1532, 4261, 4311, 9074, 10788, 220, 17, 15, 15, 8592, 13826, 311, 6481, 551, 862, 31340, 13, 1988, 807, 646, 944, 990, 678, 315, 1105, 1576, 1052, 525, 1172, 220, 16, 20, 31340, 13, 8886, 6118, 3880, 220, 16, 17, 501, 8592, 13826, 11, 323, 582, 1184, 311, 1477, 1246, 1657, 20006]}
