alon are not clients?\"\n\nSo, 210 fingers imply 21 people. But the problem says the salon made $200.00, which is for 21 clients? Or maybe the total number of clients is 21. Therefore, if there are 210 fingers, which is 21 people, and all 21 are clients, then the salon made 21 clients, each paying 20 dollars, which would be 21*20=420, not 200. But the problem says it made 200, which is not matching. Therefore, there must be a mistake here.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem says that the total amount made is $200, which is 200, but if each client is paid $20, then total number of clients is 200 / 20 = 10, which would match. But then if there are 210 fingers, that implies 21 people, which would be 21 clients. But they only have 10 clients. Therefore, there's a contradiction here.\n\nThis suggests that the problem might have conflicting information. Alternatively, maybe \"everyone has 10 fingers\" implies that 10 fingers per person, so total fingers would be 10 * number of people, which is 210, so number of people is 21. But then how many clients are there? The problem says the salon made $200.00. If there are 21 clients, but 21 clients * 20 = 420, not 200. Therefore, perhaps the problem has a typo, or maybe the total made is $200 due to other factors?\n\nWait, maybe I made a wrong assumption. Let me re-express the problem:\n\n- Nail salon was completely booked at 2 pm for manicures. So, all the clients are in the salon.\n\n- Each manicure costs $20.00 per client, so total amount made per manicure is $20.00 per client. Therefore, if there are N clients, total amount made is N * $20.00 per client.\n\nBut the problem says \"the salon made $200.00\" which would mean N * 20.00 = 200.00, so N = 10 clients.\n\nBut then the problem also says there are 210 fingers in the salon. If each person has 10 fingers, number of people is 210 / 10", "source_record": {"question": "A nail salon was completely booked at 2 pm for manicures.  Each manicure costs $20.00 per client so the salon made $200.00.  If there are 210 fingers in the salon at 2 pm, and everyone has 10 fingers, how many people in the salon are not clients?", "answer": "The salon made $200.00 and they charge $20.00 per client so there are 200/20 = <<200/20=10>>10 clients in the salon\nThere are 210 fingers in the salon and everyone has 10 fingers so there are 210/10 = <<210/10=21>>21 people in the salon\nIf there are 21 people in the salon and 10 are clients then there are 21-10 = <<21-10=11>>11 people in the salon that are not clients\n#### 11", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: A nail salon was completely booked at 2 pm for manicures.  Each manicure costs $20.00 per client so the salon made $200.00.  If there are 210 fingers in the salon at 2 pm, and everyone has 10 fingers, how many people in the salon are not clients?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["11"], "solution": "11"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 362, 30995, 39728, 572, 6587, 32970, 518, 220, 17, 8836, 369, 69122, 1413, 13, 220, 8886, 69122, 552, 7049, 400, 17, 15, 13, 15, 15, 817, 2943, 773, 279, 39728, 1865, 400, 17, 15, 15, 13, 15], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 30995, 39728, 572, 6587, 32970, 518, 220, 17, 8836, 369, 69122, 1413, 13, 8886, 69122, 552, 7049, 400, 17, 15, 13, 15, 15, 817, 2943, 11, 773, 807, 1865, 400, 17, 15, 15, 13, 15, 15, 2790, 13, 2619, 525, 220, 17, 16, 15, 19225, 304, 279, 39728]}
